 | Performance overlay<br>`checkbox_enable_perf_overlay` | Main | Off | Off; Compact; Statistics; Debug | Choose Compact, Statistics or Debug while diagnosing frame rate, network loss or delay; Off hides the overlay. Compact is one line: rendered FPS, network round trip (RTT) and frame loss behind a green, amber or red dot. Statistics summarizes the stream with a status line of lasting facts. Debug shows detailed measured stages and is always available. Stored as `checkbox_enable_perf_overlay` (On for any choice but Off) and `performance_overlay_mode` (compact, statistics or debug; Off keeps the last mode). Can also be changed in the stream menu → Display → Overlay and diagnostics; Copy stats includes Debug details. |
 | Overlay position<br>`performance_overlay_position` | More | Top left | Top left; Top right; Bottom left; Bottom right | Choose the corner the performance overlay starts in. It moves to a free corner when on-screen controls would cover it, and always stays inside the camera cutout. Right-hand corners align the text to the right. Can also be changed in the stream menu → Display → Overlay and diagnostics → Position, which takes effect at once. |
 | Picture in picture<br>`checkbox_enable_pip` | More | Off | On; Off | Enable to keep a small video window when leaving the app. Input and overlay are hidden there; requires device support. |
+| Dual screen mode<br>`checkbox_dual_screen` | More | Off | On; Off | Enable on a device with a second screen to stream the same game to both: the second screen gets a stream of its own at its own resolution, while sound, controllers and microphone stay with the first and a touch mode change on either screen applies to both. The second stream is the same device as the first, so the PC pairs once. It needs a Rubylight host that supports it, which decides which of its screens each stream shows. Applies to the next stream. |
+| Second screen resolution<br>`list_resolution_screen2` | More | Second screen's own size | Second screen's own size; 360p; 480p; 720p; 1080p; 1440p; 4K | The resolution of the second screen's stream in Dual screen mode, apart from the first screen's: the second screen's own full size, or a standard size. Applies to the next stream. Requires Dual screen mode On. |
 | Recover interrupted streams<br>`checkbox_auto_reconnect` | Main | On | On; Off | On by default. Resume the same running game after transport failures or returning from screen lock, up to five attempts within one minute. Back or leaving during a retry cancels it. Graceful termination, pairing, permissions and decoder failures stay manual; recovery never launches or replaces a game. Installs that stored the old default (off) were switched on once; turning it off again is kept. |
 | Ride out network drops<br>`list_network_grace` | More | Off (10 seconds) | Off (10 seconds); 20 seconds; 30 seconds; 60 seconds | Off by default: the stream ends after 10 seconds without contact. 20, 30 or 60 seconds keeps it open through a Wi-Fi roam, a short dropout or a VPN moving between Wi-Fi and mobile data; the picture freezes until the network returns. Longer waits only help if the host waits too, so raise its own client timeout. When the wait runs out the stream ends with a message saying so, and Recover interrupted streams, if on, then reconnects. See [network drops](video-and-latency.md#network-drops). |
 | Client roaming<br>`checkbox_client_roaming` | More | On | On; Off | On by default. When this device changes networks, the stream moves to the new address instead of waiting for the old one. Needs the New streaming engine and a PC that offers client roaming (Rubylight 3.0); other PCs keep the network grace period. |
